:: Robin Give Money [exitCheckBypass]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<div id="giveArea">
<<if $money lt 100>>
	You don't have any money to give right now.
	<br><br>
	<<link "Back">><<replace "#giveArea">><<robinoptions>><</replace>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Robin has <span class="gold">£<<print Math.max($robinmoney, 0)>></span> saved. Bailey takes <span class="gold">£<<print robinStandRent()>></span> from <<nnpc_him "Robin">> every week.
	<<if $robindebt gt 0>><span class="red"><<nnpc_Hes "Robin">> already <<print $robindebt>> week<<if $robindebt gt 1>>s<</if>> behind.</span><</if>>
	<br><br>
	You have <span class="gold"><<printmoney $money>></span>. How much would you like to give Robin to help pay Bailey?
	<br><br>
	<div id="giveInput">
		<<numberbox "_giveAmount" 1>>
		<br>
	</div>
	<div id="giveExit">
		<<link "Give">>
			<<set _giveAmount to Math.clamp(Math.trunc(_giveAmount), 1, Math.floor($money / 100))>>
			<<replace "#giveExit">><<robinGiveMoneyConfirm>><</replace>><<replace "#giveInput">><</replace>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
		<<link "Cancel">><<replace "#giveArea">><<robinoptions>><</replace>><</link>>
	</div>
<</if>>
</div>
<br>

:: Robin Give Money Done
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
Robin looks at the money you have given <<him>>, then looks up at you as though <<hes>> still trying to understand why you gave it to <<him>>.
<<if $daily.robin.giveMoney isnot 1>>
	<<set $daily.robin.giveMoney to 1>>
	"I-I don't know what to say," <<he>> says, <<his>> voice unsteady. "This really helps. It means Bailey won't... thank you. Truly." <<He>> pulls you into a tight hug.
	<br><br>
	When <<he>> lets go, <<he>> looks down at the money instead of meeting your eyes. "I just wish I didn't <i>need</i> it," <<he>> says quietly. "I should be able to manage on my own. Everyone else does." <<He>> holds the money close, but <<his>> excitement has faded.
	<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<npcincr Robin trauma -1>><<glove>><<lldom>><<lrtrauma>>
<<else>>
	"Thank you, again," <<he>> says quietly, tucking it safely away. <<He>> stares at the floor. "I'll make it count, I promise."
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>
<br>

:: Robin Stand Business
<<robinStandLocation $robinStandVenue>><<effects>>
<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinStand()>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<set _tier to setup.robinStand.tiers[$robinStand.tier]>>
<<set _drinkKey to $robinStandVenue is "park" ? "cocoa" : "lemonade">>
<<if $robinStand.named>>
	You notice <span class="gold"><<print $robinStand.named>></span>, the name Robin has painted on the front of <<his>> <<print _tier.name>>. <<Hes>> busy serving a customer.
<<else>>
	You stop to look at Robin's <<print _tier.name>> while <<he>> serves a customer.
<</if>>
<<if $robinStand.skill gte 800>>
	Robin pours the drinks and counts the customer's change quickly, without having to stop and check what <<hes>> doing.
<<elseif $robinStand.skill gte 500>>
	<<He>> takes orders and prepares drinks quickly, only stopping now and then to check what comes next.
<<elseif $robinStand.skill gte 200>>
	<<Hes>> getting better at serving customers, although <<he>> still gets nervous when several people are waiting at once.
<<else>>
	<<He>> has trouble counting the customer's change and checks the coins again before handing them over. "Sorry," <<he>> says.
<</if>>
<<robinStandBusinessBeat>>
"I made about <span class="gold">£<<print $robinStand.lastIncome>></span> last weekend,"
<<he>> says<<if $robinStand.lastIncome gte 1000>>, smiling proudly as <<he>> tells you<<elseif $robinStand.lastIncome lte 200>>, looking down at the counter as <<he>> tells you<</if>>.
"And I've got <span class="gold">£<<print Math.max($robinmoney, 0)>></span> saved under the counter."
<<if $robinStand.selfSufficient is 1>>
	<br><br>
	"I pay Bailey myself now, using what I earn here." Robin smiles as <<he>> says it, clearly pleased that <<he>> can pay <<his>> own rent.
<</if>>
<<robinCafeNotice>>
<<if robinOutfitWorn()>>
	<br><br>
	Robin is working at the stall in the <<= $robinCafe.outfit.name>> you gave <<him>>.
	<<if $robinCafe.outfit.sexy>>
		Several customers keep looking at <<him>> while they wait to order. Some of them seem more interested in Robin than the drinks.
	<<elseif $robinCafe.outfit.crossdress>>
		<<He>> wears it openly while serving customers, even with people from town passing by.
	<<else>>
		The outfit suits the stall, making <<him>> look ready for work.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $robinStand.upgrades.length gt 0>>
	You can see the extra things Robin has bought for the stand:
	<<for _i to 0; _i lt $robinStand.upgrades.length; _i++>>
		<<set _owned to robinStandUpgrade($robinStand.upgrades[_i])>>
		<<if _owned>><<print _owned[_drinkKey]>><<if _i lt $robinStand.upgrades.length - 1>>,<<else>>.<</if>><</if>>
	<</for>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set _purchases to robinStandAvailablePurchases()>>
<<if _purchases.length gt 0>>
	"There's so much I'd love to do with this stand," Robin says. <<He>> points out the things <<he>> wants to buy and explains how they would help.
	<<if !robinStandAutoUpgradeEligible()>>
		"But I can't afford them yet. Bailey takes so much of what I earn that I barely have any money left to save."
	<<else>>
		"I've managed to save some money for these lately, thanks to you."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<for _p range _purchases>>
		<<capture _p>>
			<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(_p.cost * 100, "robin")>>
				<<shopicon "register">><<link `"Fund the " + _p.name + " (" + formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_p.cost * 100)) + ")"` "Robin Stand Buy">>
					<<endevent>><<set $phase to _p.id>><<money `-(_p.cost * 100)` "robin">><</link>><<note `"+£" + _p.income + " base income a week"` "green">>
				<br>
			<<else>>
				<span class="grey">Fund the <<print _p.name>> (<<printprice `_p.cost * 100`>>)</span><<note `"+£" + _p.income + " base income a week"` "grey">>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<</capture>>
	<</for>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	"I don't think there's anything left to improve," Robin says, looking over the stall in disbelief. "It's perfect."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<robinOutfitOptions>>
<<if robinStandNamingReady()>>
	<<assignmenticon>><<link [[Help Robin name the stand (0:20)|Robin Stand Naming]]>><<pass 20>><<endevent>><</link>><<note "+5% base income a week" "green">>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$daily.robin.standTrain and $robinStand.skill lt 1000>>
	<<icon "kitchen-messy.png">><<link [[Give Robin pointers (0:30)|Robin Stand Train]]>><<pass 30>><<endevent>><</link>><<note "Trains Robin's serving skill" "green">>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<robinStandOptions $robinStandVenue>>
<br>

:: Robin Stand Buy
<<robinStandLocation $robinStandVenue>><<effects>>
<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinStand()>>
<<set _boughtTier to $phase is "tier">>
<<if _boughtTier>>
	<<set _name to setup.robinStand.tiers[Math.min($robinStand.tier + 1, 4)].name>>
<<else>>
	<<set _bought to robinStandUpgrade($phase)>>
	<<set _name to _bought ? _bought[$robinStandVenue is "park" ? "cocoa" : "lemonade"] : "upgrade">>
<</if>>
<<run robinStandBuy(V.phase)>>
<<if _boughtTier>>
	You tell Robin you're paying for the <<print _name>> <<hes>> been dreaming about. <<He>> stares at you, mouth open.
	<br><br>
	"You can't— that's so much money!" <<He>> looks at you, then back at the stand <<he>> has been using.
	"I'll pay you back. In drinks. It might take a hundred years."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> laughs and throws <<his>> arms around you. When <<he>> lets go, though, <<he>> looks back at the stand and grows quiet.
	"One day I'll buy something like this myself," <<he>> says. "You'll see."
	<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<npcincr Robin trauma -3>><<glove>><<ldom>><<llrtrauma>>
<<else>>
	You hand Robin the money for the <<print _name>>. <<He>> tries to refuse at first, but you press it into <<his>> hands.
	<br><br>
	"Thank you," <<he>> says. "You'll be the first to try the difference. On the house. Forever."
	<<He>> looks at the money for another moment before tucking it away carefully. <<Hes>> grateful for your help, but wishes <<he>> could have paid for the equipment with money from <<his>> own sales.
	<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<glove>><<ldom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinStandOptions $robinStandVenue>>
<br>

:: Robin Stand Train
<<robinStandLocation $robinStandVenue>><<effects>>
<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinStand()>>
<<set $daily.robin.standTrain to 1>>
<<set _housekeeping to currentSkillValue("housekeeping")>>
<<set _gain to 5 + Math.floor(_housekeeping / 100)>>
<<run V.robinStand.skill = Math.min(V.robinStand.skill + T.gain, 1000)>>
<<if _housekeeping gte 700>>
	You spend some time helping Robin behind the counter. You show <<him>> how to prepare drinks in the order customers need them, count change quickly, and speak to people who have been waiting a long time.
	<br><br>
	"How do you make it look so easy?" Robin asks. <<He>> follows your example, trying each task several times until <<he>> can do it without stopping to think.
<<elseif _housekeeping gte 300>>
	You join Robin behind the counter and show <<him>> how you keep the cups and supplies in order. With everything easier to reach, you and Robin serve the waiting customers more quickly.
	<br><br>
	"That's clever!" Robin says, rearranging the cups the way you showed <<him>>.
<<else>>
	You join Robin behind the counter. You're not much more experienced than <<hes>>,
	but working through the mistakes together still teaches you both something.
	<br><br>
	"We'll figure it out," Robin says with a laugh as <<he>> wipes up a drink that was spilled on the counter.
<</if>>
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>><<lstress>><<stress -3>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold"><i>Robin seems more capable behind the stand.</i></span>
<br>
<<robinStandOptions $robinStandVenue>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Renovation
<<endevent>><<effects>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set $robinCafe.seen.renovation to true>>
You tell Robin you heard that the Ocean Breeze is closed while Sam makes the cafe bigger. Since Robin can't work there until it reopens, you ask what <<he>> thinks about having some time away from the job.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 60>>
	"Have you seen how much bigger it's going to be?" Robin asks, leaning forward. "Sam will need people who know what they're doing. I could ask for more hours."
	<<He>> grins. "Maybe I'll finally earn enough to put some aside after paying Bailey."
<<elseif C.npc.Robin.dom gte 30>>
	"I'll miss getting paid while the cafe is closed," Robin says. "But there'll be more tables when it opens again. More customers, too."
	<<He>> smiles at you. "Do you think Sam would let me work more hours? I think I could manage it."
<<else>>
	"Sam said it's only until the work's finished," Robin says, pulling at the edge of <<his>> sleeve. "I know that. I just liked knowing I'd get paid."
	<<He>> looks up. "It's going to be bigger, isn't it? Maybe there'll be more work for me. As long as I can keep up."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"I've still got the stand at weekends. <<if Time.schoolTerm>>During the week I'll be here after school.<<else>>I'll be here in the afternoons during the week.<</if>> You can come round, if you want."
<br><br>
<<link [[Encourage Robin to ask for more hours|Robin Cafe Renovation Response]]>><<set $phase to "encourage">><</link>><br>
<<link [[Tell Robin you're glad to have more time together|Robin Cafe Renovation Response]]>><<set $phase to "company">><</link>><br>
<<link [[Suggest waiting to see how the new cafe goes|Robin Cafe Renovation Response]]>><<set $phase to "wait">><</link>><br>

:: Robin Cafe Renovation Response
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "encourage">>
	"You've already learnt the job," you say. "Ask Sam when it opens."
	<br><br>
	<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 30>>
		Robin nods. "I will. I'll ask what hours are available before the new people take them all."
	<<else>>
		"I suppose asking can't hurt," Robin says. <<He>> stops pulling at <<his>> sleeve and looks at you. "I'll try."
	<</if>>
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>>
<<elseif $phase is "company">>
	You tell Robin you'll enjoy having more afternoons together.
	<br><br>
	"You will?" <<He>> smiles<<if C.npc.Robin.dom lt 30>>, glancing down at <<his>> hands<<else>> and makes room beside <<him>><</if>>. "I'd like that too."
	<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<<else>>
	"Try the new cafe before you ask for extra shifts," you suggest. "You'll have more tables to look after."
	<br><br>
	Robin nods. "That's true. I don't want to promise Sam hours I can't manage. I'll see how it goes."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Ask Sam
<<endevent>><<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Sam>><<person1>><<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You wait until there are no customers at the counter, then ask Sam if there's any work for a friend of yours.
"A friend?" Sam asks. "How old?"
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> Robin's age. Sam thinks for a few seconds before answering.
"Same age as you, then. Can <<nnpc_he "Robin">> work weekday afternoons?"
<br><br>
You say yes.
<br><br>
Sam turns towards the sheet of paper beside Old Betsy that lists everyone's working hours. There are still several afternoons with no one assigned to work.
"I could use the help. But <<nnpc_he "Robin">> needs to handle customers. Some of them get rude when they're angry or impatient."
 <br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> works really hard," you say quietly. "<<nnpc_Hes "Robin">> been serving customers at <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own drinks stand since <<nnpc_he "Robin">> was small."
	<<case "shy">>
		You speak softly, but make sure Sam hears you. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> runs a drinks stand without anyone helping. <<nnpc_He "Robin">> already knows how to serve customers."
	<<case "polite">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> has experience serving customers," you explain. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> sells lemonade in warm weather and cocoa in winter, and makes the signs for <<nnpc_his "Robin">> stand too."
	<<case "neutral">>
		You explain that Robin runs a drinks stand, selling lemonade when it's warm and cocoa when it's cold. <<nnpc_He "Robin">> makes the signs and serves customers without anyone helping.
	<<case "confident">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> can handle customers," you tell Sam. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> already runs a drinks stand alone, takes orders and makes <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own signs."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">>'ll be fine," you say. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> already runs <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own drinks stand. <<nnpc_He "Robin">> isn't going to fall apart because someone's rude."
	<<case "docile">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> knows how to work with customers," you say gently. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> has a drinks stand and takes care of the orders and signs without anyone helping."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> has experience serving customers," you explain. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> sells lemonade in warm weather and cocoa in winter, and makes the signs for <<nnpc_his "Robin">> stand too."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> can deal with a few rude customers," you say. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> runs a drinks stand alone. <<nnpc_He "Robin">> knows how to take orders without needing someone to do it for <<nnpc_him "Robin">>."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Ask Sam 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Ask Sam 2
<<effects>>
Sam listens with <<his>> arms folded. By the time you finish, <<hes>> smiling.
"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> runs <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own stall already?"
<br><br>
Sam thinks about it, then nods. "Bring <<nnpc_him "Robin">> in. I'll give <<nnpc_him "Robin">> two weeks to try the job.
If <<nnpc_he "Robin">> does well, <<nnpc_he "Robin">> can stay."
<br><br>
<<He>> points towards the tables. "And tell <<nnpc_him "Robin">> that any tips customers give <<nnpc_him "Robin">>
are <<nnpc_his "Robin">> to keep. We don't share tips between the staff here."
<br><br>
<span class="gold"><i>Sam has a place for Robin. You need to tell Robin about it.</i></span>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell
<<endevent>><<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>><<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You tell Robin about the job Sam has offered <<him>> at the Ocean Breeze. Robin sits with you and listens without interrupting, even when you explain that Sam wants <<him>> to try the job for two weeks first.
<br><br>
"A real job," <<he>> says when you finish. "I'd get paid every week, and I'd know which days I'm working."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks down at <<his>> hands.
"I've been thinking about how much I'd earn while you were talking. We'd still be okay. I know that."
<<He>> rubs <<his>> palms against <<his>> knees. "But what if I'm bad at it?"
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"You've been running your own stand since you were nine," you say softly. "I think you can learn this too."
	<<case "shy">>
		You give Robin a small smile. "You've worked at your stand for years. You'll have two weeks to learn the cafe job."
	<<case "polite">>
		"You're allowed to make mistakes while you're learning," you tell <<him>>. "Sam has given you two weeks to try the job."
	<<case "neutral">>
		"Then you'll learn," you say. "That's what the two-week trial is for."
	<<case "confident">>
		"You can do this," you tell <<him>>. "You've handled your own stand for years, and Sam's giving you time to learn."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Then you'll be bad at it for two weeks and Sam'll tell you," you say. "That's why <<nnpc_he "Sam">> gave you a trial."
	<<case "docile">>
		"That's okay," you say. "You can take your time learning. Sam knows you're new."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"You're allowed to make mistakes while you're learning," you tell <<him>>. "Sam has given you two weeks to try the job."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"Nobody starts out knowing everything," you say. "If you mess up, you fix it and try again. That's what the trial is for."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Tell 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell 2
<<effects>>
Robin stays quiet for a few seconds, then starts counting the days on <<his>> fingers.
"Only weekdays... So I can still run the stand at weekends."
<<He>> looks up at you.
"I wouldn't have to give it up."
<br><br>
Robin stands up from the bed so quickly that <<he>> nearly falls over. <<He>> grabs the side of the bed with one hand to keep <<himself>> upright.
<br><br>
"Okay," <<he>> says. "Tell Sam yes."
<<He>> pauses, then shakes <<his>> head.
"No. I'll tell <<nnpc_him "Sam">> myself. I should do that."
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<glove>><<ggdom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Tell 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell 3
<<effects>>
<<if robinCafeClosed()>>
	Robin's job at the Ocean Breeze will wait <span class="gold">until the cafe reopens</span>. After that, <<he>> will work on school days, from five until seven.
<<else>>
	Robin starts work at the Ocean Breeze <span class="gold">on the next school day</span>, from five until seven.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Once Robin starts working shifts, <<he>> will spend less time preparing for the stand, <span class="purple">so the stand will earn less money.</span>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 2>><<set $robinCafe.startTime to Time.date.timeStamp>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Visit
<<endevent>><<effects>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set _due to robinCafeSceneDue()>>
<<set _outfitDue to robinOutfitSceneDue()>>
<<if _due or _outfitDue>>
	The cafe is busy. You make your way through it towards the counter.
	<br><br>
	<<if _due is "first">>
		<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift]]>><</link>>
	<<elseif _due is "difficult">>
		<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult]]>><</link>>
	<<elseif _outfitDue is "debut">>
		<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Debut]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Regulars]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if robinOutfitWorn()>>
		<<robinOutfitLook>>
	<<else>>
		Robin stands behind the counter wearing an apron that is too long for <<him>>.
		Sam has folded it over twice at the waist to make it fit.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $robinCafe.stage gte 5 and $robinCafe.ended is "kept">>
		Robin takes a customer's order and passes it to the kitchen. On <<his>> way back to the counter, <<he>> collects two empty plates from a table before going to serve the next customer.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> spots you while carrying the plates and gives you a quick grin before continuing back to the counter.
	<<elseif $robinCafe.stage gte 3>>
		Robin serves the last few people waiting at the counter, entering each order into the machine that records sales before speaking to the next customer.
		<br><br>
		When there are no more customers waiting, <<he>> comes over to you. The coffee machine is still making a drink behind <<him>>.
		"Eleven tables since five! I counted."
	<<else>>
		Robin is working at the machine that records orders, reading each button carefully before pressing it. <<Hes>> so busy checking the screen that <<he>> does not notice you until you reach the counter.
		<br><br>
		When <<he>> looks up and sees you, <<he>> forgets which part of the order <<he>> was entering.
		<<He>> looks back at the screen and starts it again from the beginning with flushed cheeks.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if !$daily.robin.cafeVisit>>
		<<set $daily.robin.cafeVisit to 1>>
		Robin places a drink in front of you even though you did not order anything.
		"Staff discount! On me. I get one every shift and I never use it."
		<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		Robin keeps moving between the machine that records orders and the drinks waiting to be served.
		You decide not to distract <<him>> while <<hes>> working.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<robinOutfitOptions>>
	<<link [[Leave <<him>> to it|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>><<set $robinCafe.seen.first to true>>
You find Robin carrying two plates while four customers wait near the counter.
A third plate is ready beside Sam, but Robin keeps looking between the food in <<his>> hands and the table numbers.
<br><br>
Sam prepares another order behind the counter. "Table six!" Sam calls.
<br><br>
Robin starts walking towards the tables, repeating "six" quietly to <<himself>> so <<he>> will remember where to take the food.
<br><br>
"Two coffees for table three!" Sam calls after <<him>>.
<br><br>
Robin looks back at Sam, and the new order makes <<him>> forget which table <<he>> was looking for. <<He>> hesitates, then walks to the nearest table with customers and puts both plates down.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 2
<<effects>>
One of the customers looks at the food. "We didn't order these."
<br><br>
Robin freezes, then quickly picks the plates back up.
"Sorry. Sorry..."
<br><br>
<<He>> turns towards the other tables with a plate in each hand, but stops after a few steps. <<He>> looks from one plate to the other, trying to remember which food belongs at which table.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40>>
	Robin carries both plates back to the counter and puts them down.
	<<He>> takes a slow breath, then returns to the customers.
	"Sorry. Do you know which table ordered these?"
	<br><br>
	One of the customers points towards another table. Robin checks the table number with Sam, then carries the plates to the people who ordered them.
	<br><br>
	When <<he>> returns, <<he>> looks at the now-empty space where the plates were, surprised that asking for help solved the problem.
<<else>>
	Robin's ears turn red. <<He>> carries both plates back to the counter and places them beside Sam, avoiding the customers' eyes as <<he>> walks away.
	"Sorry," <<he>> says again, though nobody has spoken to <<him>>.
	<br><br>
	Sam checks the plates, points towards the correct tables, and sends <<him>> back out.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 3
<<effects>>
The cafe is still open, but there are fewer people waiting to order now. Robin finishes clearing a table and finally has time to stop working for a moment.
<br><br>
<<He>> comes over to you after clearing another table. There is an empty chair beside you, but <<he>> remains standing.
"That was awful," <<he>> says. "...I was awful."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"You stayed until the end," you say softly. "I think that's enough for your first day."
		<br><br>
		Robin looks back towards the counter before giving a small nod.
	<<case "shy">>
		"You made it through the whole shift," you say, giving <<him>> a small smile. "You'll get better with practice."
		<br><br>
		Robin looks back towards the counter before giving a small nod.
	<<case "polite">>
		"It was your first day," you remind <<him>>. "You had a lot to learn, but you stayed and finished your work."
		<br><br>
		Robin smiles a little, though <<he>> still looks embarrassed.
	<<case "neutral">>
		"You were new," you say. "Tomorrow you'll know more than you did today."
		<br><br>
		Robin pulls a face, but <<he>> does not argue.
	<<case "confident">>
		"You made mistakes, but you sorted them out," you say. "Tomorrow will be easier because you've done it once already."
		<br><br>
		Robin nods, looking a little more willing to believe you.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"You were," you say. "Really bad. And you're doing it again tomorrow."
		<br><br>
		Robin stares at you, then laughs when <<he>> realises you're teasing <<him>>.
	<<case "docile">>
		"It was a difficult day," you say gently. "You can rest now, and try again tomorrow."
		<br><br>
		Robin looks over towards the counter, then nods.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"It was your first day," you remind <<him>>. "You had a lot to learn, but you stayed and finished your work."
		<br><br>
		Robin smiles a little, though <<he>> still looks embarrassed.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"You messed up some orders," you say. "But you fixed them and finished the shift, so stop acting like the whole day was a failure."
		<br><br>
		Robin looks at you in surprise, then gives a reluctant nod.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 4
<<effects>>
Sam looks over from behind the counter while Robin is busy elsewhere. Sam gives you a small shrug, points towards Robin, and smiles as though to say that it's normal to make mistakes on the first day.
<br><br>
Robin got through the first shift.
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin trauma 2>><<glove>><<grtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
