:: Robin Cafe Difficult
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<person1>><<generates2>><<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You have only just entered the cafe when you hear someone shouting near the counter. A <<person2>><<persons>> standing in front of Robin, with a cup on the counter between them.
<br><br>
<<He>> points at the drink as <<he>> speaks.
"I asked for no milk. Twice! Did you enter the order wrong, or did the machine make a mistake?"
<br><br>
<<person1>>Robin stands behind the counter, pressing both hands against it. <<He>> looks at the customer without answering. Sam is in the kitchen with the door shut, and people at two nearby tables have stopped talking so they can watch what happens.
Robin still hasn't apologised. Usually, <<he>> would have done that already.
<br><br>
<<link [[Step in|Robin Cafe Difficult Step]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay where you are|Robin Cafe Difficult Wait]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Step
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.handled to "player">>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 4>>
Before Robin can answer, you walk over and stand beside <<him>> behind the counter. You take the customer's cup from the counter.
<br><br>
"Sorry about that," you say. You pour away the drink, then make a new one without adding milk. The customer watches while you work.
<br><br>
The <<person2>><<person>> waits until you have finished making the new drink before taking it. <<He>> complains that the cafe should be more careful with orders, then carries the cup over to a table.
<<person1>>Robin stays beside you the whole time. <<He>> does not interrupt or try to take over.
<br><br>
Once the customer has walked away, Robin looks down at <<his>> apron. <<He>> reaches behind <<his>> back, unties the apron strings, then ties them again more slowly.
"Thanks," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<He>> keeps <<his>> attention on the apron for another second before looking up.
"I think I could've handled that. I was trying to work out what to say."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult Step 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Step 2
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"I'm sorry," you say quietly. "I didn't think before stepping in."
	<<case "shy">>
		You look down at the counter. "Sorry. I should've asked if you wanted help."
	<<case "polite">>
		"You're right, and I'm sorry," you say. "I thought I was helping, but I should have let you answer the customer."
	<<case "neutral">>
		"I know," you say. "I just didn't want you to have to deal with <<him>>."
	<<case "confident">>
		"I know you could have handled it," you say. "I stepped in because the customer was being rude, but I should have let you try."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"You were taking your time about it," you say. Robin looks hurt, and you realise the joke didn't come out the way you meant it.
	<<case "docile">>
		"I'm sorry," you say. "You should have had the chance to answer. I won't jump in so quickly next time."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"You're right, and I'm sorry," you say. "I thought I was helping, but I should have let you answer the customer."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"You were taking a while," you say. "But I should've let you deal with <<him>> yourself. You need the practice."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Robin lets go of <<his>> apron. "That's the problem. People always try to handle difficult customers for me because they don't think I can do it. I need to learn how to deal with them myself."
<br><br>
<<He>> picks up a cloth and walks over to an empty table. There are only a few crumbs on it,
but <<he>> wipes them away anyway.<<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<lldom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Wait
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.handled to "robin">>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 4>>
You stay near the cafe entrance instead of going up to the counter. You want to help Robin, especially with the other customers watching, but you give <<him>> a chance to answer for <<himself>>.
<br><br>
Robin takes the cup from <<person2>>the <<person>> without arguing.
"I'll make you another one. It'll take about a minute. You can sit down while you wait, or stay here.
Which do you want?"
<br><br>
<<person2>>The <<person>> starts to answer, then stops. <<He>> looks at the nearby chair, then back at Robin.
After a few seconds, <<he>> pulls the chair out and sits down.
<br><br>
Robin turns back to the counter and makes the drink again. When it's ready, <<person1>><<he>>
carries it over and places it in front of <<person2>>the <<person>>. "Here you go."
<br><br>
<<person1>><<He>> walks back to the counter before <<person2>>the <<person>> can start complaining again.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult Wait 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Wait 2
<<effects>>
The people at the two nearby tables watch for another few seconds. When nothing else happens,
they turn back to their drinks and conversations.
<br><br>
<<person1>>You walk over to Robin. <<His>> hands shake slightly as <<he>> puts the used cup aside.
When <<he>> notices you looking, <<he>> lowers them behind the counter.
"I've watched Sam do that about ten times. If you give an angry customer two choices, they have to stop shouting long enough to decide what they want."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"That was really good," you say softly.
		<br><br>
		Robin looks down for a second, but this time <<he>> doesn't argue with the praise.
	<<case "shy">>
		"You did really well," you say, smiling at <<him>>.
		<br><br>
		Robin looks down for a second, but this time <<he>> doesn't argue with the praise.
	<<case "polite">>
		"You handled that well," you tell <<him>>. "You stayed calm even when the customer was shouting."
		<br><br>
		Robin nods, still looking surprised that it worked.
	<<case "neutral">>
		"You didn't need me," you say.
		<br><br>
		Robin pauses before answering. "No," <<he>> says, sounding a little surprised by it too.
	<<case "confident">>
		"See? You handled it yourself," you say. "You knew what to say."
		<br><br>
		Robin smiles, still looking surprised that it worked.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Look at you," you say. "Terrifying."
		<br><br>
		"Shut up," <<he>> says, smiling.
	<<case "docile">>
		"You did well," you say gently. "I knew you could manage."
		<br><br>
		Robin looks at <<his>> hands, then gives you a small smile.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"You handled that well," you tell <<him>>. "You stayed calm even when the customer was shouting."
		<br><br>
		Robin nods, still looking surprised that it worked.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"That customer wanted an argument, and you didn't give <<him>> one," you say. "You handled it better than <<he>> deserved."
		<br><br>
		Robin smiles a little, pleased that you noticed.
<</switch>>
<<npcincr Robin dom 6>><<gggdom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
