:: Robin Cafe Shortage
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You step behind the cafe counter and see Robin squeezing an empty carton in <<his>> hands. You take it from <<him>> before <<he>> crushes it.
"Come with me," you say. "Just for a minute."
<br><br>
You lead <<him>> into the staff room and shut the door. Robin turns to you as soon as you are alone.
"We've run out of $phase," <<he>> says. "I checked the fridge and the shelf beside the machine, but I couldn't find any more."
<br><br>
<<He>> rubs <<his>> hands against <<his>> apron.
<br><br>
"I was supposed to tell Sam when we opened the last one. I didn't realise it was the last carton until just now."
<<He>> looks back towards the door. "People have already ordered drinks that need it. I don't know what to tell them."
<br><br>
<<link [[Help Robin calm down and work out what to do|Robin Cafe Shortage Reassure]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Cover the counter while Robin buys more|Robin Cafe Shortage Cover]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(1000, "cafe")>>
	<<link [[Go and buy more yourself|Robin Cafe Shortage Fetch]]>><<money -1000 "cafe">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $chef_state gte 1>>
	<<link [[Use something else from the kitchen|Robin Cafe Shortage Substitute]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Cafe Shortage Continue
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You return to your tables. Several customers are still waiting for their orders,
so you keep working instead of stopping to help Robin.
<br><br>
Later, you pass the counter again and see Sam standing beside Robin.
Robin's face turns red while Sam writes <i>CHECK THE LAST CARTON</i> on the sheet used to record the cafe's supplies. Sam draws two lines under the words to make sure Robin notices them.
<br><br>
"Running out of something isn't the end of the world," Sam says. "But you need to tell me when we're almost out, so I can buy more before we need it."
<br><br>
Robin looks at you for a second before lowering <<his>> eyes.
<<He>> turns back to the counter and continues working.<<npcincr Robin trauma 2>><<grtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<waiter_default>><<pass 1 hour>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Shortage Reassure
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
"Robin, look at me," you say.
<br><br>
<<He>> keeps looking towards the cafe for a few seconds before turning back to you.
<br><br>
"We've run out of $phase," you say. "It's a problem, but we can fix it. What should you do first?"
<br><br>
Robin opens <<his>> mouth, but no words come out. <<He>> takes a slow breath and tries again.
"Tell Sam we've run out. Then explain to the customers that they can order their drinks without $phase or choose something else. After that, I need to buy more."
<br><br>
You nod. "That's right," you say. "Talk to Sam first."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Shortage Reassure 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Shortage Reassure 2
<<effects>>
Robin follows you out of the staff room and back into the cafe. When you reach Sam, Robin slows down and looks at you, but you stay beside <<him>> and give <<him>> time to speak.
<br><br>
"We ran out of $phase," Robin says. <<His>> voice shakes, but <<he>> manages to finish.
"I didn't notice until we needed another carton."
<br><br>
Sam looks at Robin, then points towards the highest shelf in the cupboard where the cafe keeps its spare supplies. Robin looks where Sam is pointing and sees another carton of $phase there.
<br><br>
Robin stares at the carton for a few seconds, then covers <<his>> face with one hand and starts laughing. <<He>> leans against you, laughing even harder when <<he>> realises how much time <<he>> spent looking everywhere else.<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<br><br>
"I looked everywhere," <<he>> says. "I didn't look up."
<br><br>
<<waiter_default>><<pass 1 hour>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<unset $phase>><<endevent>><</link>>
